<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Dayton Hudson upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Dayton Hudson upgraded.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Securities Corp analyst Robert Buchanan upgraded Dayton Hudson Corp to accumulate from hold, according to the analyst's office.</p>
<p>Earlier, Dayton Hudson reported it earned $0.44 a share in the first quarter compared to $0.16 a share a year earlier. The results exceeded Wall Street's expectations of about $0.40 a share.</p>
<p>Buchanan also increased his estimate for Dayton Hudson's full-year earnings to $3.15 a share from $2.97 previously. In 1996, the retailer earned $463 million, or $1.95 a share, including an after-tax charge of $81 million for real estate repositioning costs and another after-tax charge of $11 million for a debt repurchase.</p>
<p>Further details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
